      <h2>Why we started</h2>
      <p>Jay Home Buyers was started to give homeowners a simpler option when a regular sale doesn’t fit. Some houses need more work than it makes sense to do before selling. Some families are settling an estate and don’t want months of showings. Sometimes life just needs to move faster than a listing allows.</p>
      <p>We saw too many sellers stuck between two bad choices: spend money they don’t have fixing up a house, or deal with buyers who make an offer and then disappear. We wanted to offer a straightforward alternative: a fair cash offer, in writing, on a timeline the seller chooses.</p>

      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <p>We buy houses for cash, as-is, in Ontario and Alberta. Sometimes we keep and renovate a house. Often we work with other investors and renovators who take on the project. Either way, your offer and your closing date are in writing, with lawyers on both sides.</p>
      <p>If buying your house ourselves isn’t a good fit, we’ll say so. With your permission, we can connect you with a licensed realtor we trust.</p>

      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Every offer is reviewed personally.</strong> No algorithm decides your number, and we explain how we got to it.</li>
        <li><strong>No pressure, ever.</strong> You get a number and the space to decide. Walking away costs you nothing.</li>
        <li><strong>Plain, honest answers.</strong> If listing with a realtor would get you more, we’ll tell you.</li>
        <li><strong>Your information stays with us.</strong> We’re not a national franchise passing your details around.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>See <a href="/how-it-works/">how the process works</a>, or read our <a href="/faq/">frequently asked questions</a>.</p>

      <p class="note">Jay Home Buyers is a private buyer, not a real estate brokerage. We don’t list or market homes on behalf of sellers.</p>
